{:event/actor "seb" :event/at #inst "2026-07-29T18:47:43.449Z" :event/body {:fact/path [:summary] :fact/value "tik set <id> price=1.5 exits 1 with 'tik: unsupported type in canonical EDN'. It fails well and writes nothing, but decimals, ratios and bigdecimals are ordinary things to type and the message names an internal layer instead of the fix. The kernel is right to reject them - floats are not byte-stable - so the porcelain should catch the rejection and say which value was refused and what to write instead (price=\"1.5\" as a string, or an integer in minor units). CLAUDE.md already forbids kernel prose leaking into user surfaces."} :event/parents #{"sha256-1852afa2594c7cb33eb67f5417269c94078edada713c5b2d62c10f988d528696"} :event/ticket #uuid "32f1250b-e2b0-4069-867e-e250daef4f17" :event/type :fact/assert}